WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.625
I'm going to talk to you

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:02.458
about the worst types of bread

00:00:02.458 --> 00:00:04.416
that you want to avoid eating,

00:00:04.416 --> 00:00:06.375
as well as some alternatives

00:00:06.375 --> 00:00:06.833
for when you're

00:00:06.833 --> 00:00:07.666
in the supermarket,

00:00:07.666 --> 00:00:08.291
when you want to make

00:00:08.291 --> 00:00:09.250
something at home.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.250
Now, bread is taking a bit

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:10.750
of a beating

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:11.666
over the last few years.

00:00:11.666 --> 00:00:13.000
It spikes your sugar.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:13.916
It could potentially cause

00:00:13.916 --> 00:00:14.708
weight gain.

00:00:14.708 --> 00:00:16.458
But is it breads for

00:00:16.458 --> 00:00:18.416
or is it the type of bread?

00:00:18.416 --> 00:00:19.208
In a word,

00:00:19.208 --> 00:00:20.083
the type of bread

00:00:20.083 --> 00:00:21.250
that you want to avoid

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.125
are supermarket breads.

00:00:23.125 --> 00:00:24.291
These are mass

00:00:24.291 --> 00:00:26.583
produced on an industrial scale

00:00:26.583 --> 00:00:28.750
with extensive automation.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:29.625
And one study

00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:30.166
that we looked

00:00:30.166 --> 00:00:31.250
at compared industrial,

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.000
artisanal and homemade breads.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:33.750
And they found that

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:34.958
artisanal bread

00:00:34.958 --> 00:00:36.541
had a lot more sugar

00:00:36.541 --> 00:00:37.541
and markers of something

00:00:37.541 --> 00:00:39.041
called a milliard reaction

00:00:39.041 --> 00:00:39.625
that we'll talk

00:00:39.625 --> 00:00:40.708
about in a second.

00:00:40.708 --> 00:00:41.625
And that makes it

00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:42.708
not as good for you.

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:43.291
In fact,

00:00:43.291 --> 00:00:43.875
something that

00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:45.541
I think you should avoid.

00:00:45.541 --> 00:00:47.208
So this is your typical

00:00:47.208 --> 00:00:48.541
supermarket bread here.

00:00:48.541 --> 00:00:49.208
Let me tell you a bit

00:00:49.208 --> 00:00:50.291
about supermarket bread.

00:00:50.291 --> 00:00:51.583
So there is a high

00:00:51.583 --> 00:00:52.583
degree of processing.

00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:55.083
So this is a processed food.

00:00:55.083 --> 00:00:56.541
It's more likely to contain

00:00:56.541 --> 00:00:58.500
additives and flavourings

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.458
mainly texture.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:01.583
It's including emulsifiers

00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:04.291
hydrocolloid, preservatives.

00:01:04.291 --> 00:01:05.416
It's going to be

00:01:05.416 --> 00:01:06.541
it's going to have a lot more

00:01:06.541 --> 00:01:07.875
things like vegetable oils

00:01:07.875 --> 00:01:08.250
and as well

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.541
that shouldn't be anywhere near

00:01:09.541 --> 00:01:10.916
a bread like sunflower

00:01:10.916 --> 00:01:11.875
or rapeseed.

00:01:11.875 --> 00:01:12.416
They contain

00:01:12.416 --> 00:01:14.375
higher amounts of sugar content

00:01:14.375 --> 00:01:16.000
because of the use of certain

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.291
ingredients, notably

00:01:17.291 --> 00:01:18.916
soybean flour,

00:01:18.916 --> 00:01:20.875
which contains more sugar

00:01:20.875 --> 00:01:22.458
than wheat flour.

00:01:22.458 --> 00:01:23.458
And then you also have

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:24.375
more markers of something

00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:25.500
called the Marriott reactions.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.833
In the Marriott reaction

00:01:26.833 --> 00:01:27.958
is a chemical reaction

00:01:27.958 --> 00:01:28.958
between proteins,

00:01:28.958 --> 00:01:30.500
your amino acids,

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.583
and reducing sugars

00:01:31.583 --> 00:01:33.250
to create melanin.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:34.291
And these are the compounds

00:01:34.291 --> 00:01:35.625
that give a distinctive

00:01:35.625 --> 00:01:36.875
aroma of flavour.

00:01:36.875 --> 00:01:38.250
It's very delicious,

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:38.625
but it could

00:01:38.625 --> 00:01:40.291
potentially increase

00:01:40.291 --> 00:01:41.875
the number of carcinogens

00:01:41.875 --> 00:01:43.583
that you find in bread as well,

00:01:43.583 --> 00:01:44.875
with potential consequences

00:01:44.875 --> 00:01:45.208
to health.

00:01:45.208 --> 00:01:47.166
So this is your

00:01:47.166 --> 00:01:49.291
typical supermarket bread here.

00:01:49.291 --> 00:01:50.458
they all pretty much

00:01:50.458 --> 00:01:51.166
look the same.

00:01:51.166 --> 00:01:52.666
They're all wrapped in plastic.

00:01:52.666 --> 00:01:53.625
You can almost tell

00:01:53.625 --> 00:01:54.208
the difference

00:01:54.208 --> 00:01:54.833
between the bread

00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:56.458
just by like weighing it

00:01:56.458 --> 00:01:57.291
in your hands.

00:01:57.291 --> 00:01:59.125
It feels very soft and spongy.

00:01:59.125 --> 00:01:59.875
There isn't really

00:01:59.875 --> 00:02:01.041
much substance to them,

00:02:01.041 --> 00:02:02.208
unfortunately.

00:02:02.208 --> 00:02:02.708
And,

00:02:02.708 --> 00:02:05.041
if you look at the ingredients

00:02:05.041 --> 00:02:05.958
and often like,

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:06.166
you know,

00:02:06.166 --> 00:02:06.791
they've got

00:02:06.791 --> 00:02:07.916
these green things saying

00:02:07.916 --> 00:02:08.708
high in fibre,

00:02:08.708 --> 00:02:10.416
rich in whole grains,

00:02:10.416 --> 00:02:11.333
just ignore that.

00:02:11.333 --> 00:02:12.500
Just just go straight

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:13.708
to the ingredients list.

00:02:13.708 --> 00:02:16.375
That is where they cannot lie.

00:02:18.083 --> 00:02:18.625
ingredients.

00:02:18.625 --> 00:02:19.458
Whole, whole

00:02:19.458 --> 00:02:20.375
mill, wheat flour,

00:02:20.375 --> 00:02:21.791
water, yeast,

00:02:21.791 --> 00:02:22.708
vegetable oils,

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:24.833
rapeseed and sustainable

00:02:24.833 --> 00:02:26.083
palm palms.

00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:27.625
Not sustainable salt,

00:02:27.625 --> 00:02:28.583
wheat gluten,

00:02:28.583 --> 00:02:33.208
emulsifiers E481471472E

